  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "trace-11a-conditions-and-on-bar",
      "title": "Condition strategy (entry_when, exit_when) with two scale-out targets, and its equivalent on_bar",
      "depends_on": ["SPEC-21", "SPEC-22", "SPEC-23", "SPEC-29"],
      "notes": [
        "This case carries the strategy in two forms that must give the same expected result. strategy.conditions is the declarative form: one boolean per strategy bar, the value of the condition at that bar's close (in Phases 1 to 3 the kernel consumes such arrays, 14-strategy-api 4.3). strategy.decisions is the equivalent on_bar of 14-strategy-api 4.1: with pyramiding 0 it reduces to 'if flat and entry_cond: buy(**entry_args)' and 'if long and exit_cond: exit()', so every true value becomes one guarded decision at that bar's close. A kernel runner executes both forms.",
        "entry_when order arguments do not include qty (14-strategy-api 4.1), so the size is given as size=bt.size.qty(100) (SPEC-23). The declarative form consuming arrays with the level-triggered semantics of 4.1 is SPEC-29.",
        "No entry bar touches a level (SPEC-02 does not matter). There is no trail. All levels are exact ticks.",
        "The run shows: no add while the entry condition stays true (pyramiding 0); exit priority in a position and entry priority when flat when both conditions are true (bars 09:35 and 09:40); the remainder after a partial target leaving by signal; and re-entry on the bar after a stop because the condition is level-triggered (bar 09:50)."
      ],
